      "body": "## Motivation\n\nTwo kinds of LLaDA-Image edit requests pass request validation and are then refused inside the worker, so the client receives a 500 response with a bare Internal Server Error body while the server stays healthy. An edit at 1920x1920 fits the 32768-row sequence limit only if the caption is left out, and an edit with more than one source image is refused only after the text encoder has already run.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Count the caption's 256 query tokens and one text token in the editing size bound, so the bound matches the check the DiT makes for short prompts. A 1920x1920 edit is now rejected while 1888x1888 is still admitted.\n- Reject more than one source image for a single prompt when the sampling parameters are built. Prompt lists and prompt files keep pairing one image with each prompt for offline generation.\n- Extend the existing validation test with the new size boundary and the two-image case.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The extended unit test fails before this change and passes with it, and the other LLaDA-Image config tests pass.\n- Across every editing size on the 32-pixel grid, the sizes that are newly rejected are exactly those the DiT refuses for every prompt, and every size that stays admitted runs with the shortest prompt.\n- On one GPU with LLaDA-Image-Turbo, the 1920x1920 edit and the two-image edit now return 400 with these messages instead of 500.\n  - `LLaDA-Image editing at 1920x1920 needs at least 32977 sequence positions, above the model limit of 32768`\n  - `LLaDA-Image editing takes exactly one source image, got 2`\n- Edits at 1888x1888 and 1024x1024 and text to image requests still succeed, health stays 200 after every refusal, and 14 text to image and edit requests return byte-identical images before and after the change.\n\n## Limits\n\nA prompt long enough to push an otherwise admitted edit past the sequence limit is still refused inside the worker with a 500 response, because request validation does not tokenize the prompt.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38117312858](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38117312858)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38117312787](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38117312787)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38117312889](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38117312889)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
